            0.397
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What will be the total cost incurred?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.397,
            0.821,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cost of wire fencing along the garden length = 2l × 100 = `200l"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.417,
            0.863,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cost of wooden fencing along the garden width "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2w \\times 80 = \\bar{x}160w"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.437,
            0.883,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cost of sowing seeds throughout the entire garden (depends on the area) = 50 × l × w = `50lw"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.474,
            0.523,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Total cost = ` (200l + 160w + 50lw)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.493,
            0.883,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, 200l + 160w + 50lw is the algebraic expression for the total cost."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.53,
            0.399,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.567,
            0.866,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Can you identify the terms, variables and coefficients of this algebraic expression?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.609,
            0.789,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. How is it different from the algebraic expression in Example 1?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.644,
            0.885,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A wire of length 20 cm is bent in different ways to form rectangles. For example, we can have a rectangle with length 7 cm and width 3 cm. We can also have one of length 5.5 cm and width 4.5 cm. (Think of a few more ways of forming such rectangles.) Can you write an expression for the area of such rectangles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.741,
            0.882,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the length of the rectangle is x cm, then the width is (10 – x) cm. The expression for the area of these rectangles is x(10 – x) or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 X - X ^ { 2 } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.796,
            0.399,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.834,
            0.866,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Can you identify the terms, variables and coefficients of this algebraic expression?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.876,
            0.866,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Can you point out any similarity or difference between the algebraic expressions obtained in Examples 1 and 3?"
